    "title": "Maryville City Schools provides free and reduced lunch to qualifying students - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Maryville City Schools has announced its policy for free and reduced price meals. According to a release from the district, children may receive free or reduced-price meals if the family's household income falls within the limits of the Federal Income Eligibility Guidelines. The release also said that all children receiving SNAP, Food Distribution Program on Indian Reservations or TANF benefits are eligible for free meals. Children in households receiving benefits from Medicaid may be eligible for free or reduced meals. The release said that when known to MCS, households will be notified of their children's eligibility for free or reduced-cost lunch. Normal meal cost is: Breakfast: $1.35 to $1.60; Lunch: $2.90 to $3.25. Reduced-cost meals are: Breakfast: $0.30; Lunch: $0.40. Call 865-982-7121 for more information. Subscribe to The Daily Times",
